---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Terms & privacy | {SITE_NAME}</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Terms of use and privacy notes for the shareatrade contractor directory. Not legal advice. Not affiliated with listed businesses or Google."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Terms & privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Plain-language rules for using {SITE_NAME}. This page is not legal advice.
      If something here doesn’t match how you need to use the directory, don’t
      rely on the site for that purpose. Last updated August 14, 2026.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who we are (and aren’t)</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE_NAME} is an independent, free directory of local trades, starting
        with Spokane.
        We are not Google, Meta, Nextdoor, Washington L&amp;I, the Washington
        Department of Labor &amp; Industries, any city or county, any insurer,
        or any contractor listed here. Listing a business does not mean we
        employ them, endorse them, inspect their work, or have a partnership
        with them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Names, logos, ratings, reviews, photos, and websites that appear on
        listings belong to their owners. We use publicly available business
        information (especially Google Business Profile) so neighbors can share
        a complete name—not because those companies asked us to speak for them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Not advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is legal, insurance, tax, financial, construction,
        or professional advice. Hiring help pages are general orientation only.
        License badges and L&amp;I lookups, when we show them, can be incomplete,
        delayed, or wrong. You still verify licensing, bonding, insurance,
        permits, and scope with the contractor, the relevant agency, and your
        insurer or adjuster before you hire or pay anyone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Using the directory</h2>
      <p>
        The directory is for personal, non-commercial browsing and sharing of
        listing links. You agree not to scrape, bulk-copy, or republish our
        database; not to misrepresent a listing as your own; and not to use
        contact details here for spam or unrelated marketing. We may add,
        edit, hide, or remove listings at any time, including when a Google
        Business Profile changes or a request looks inaccurate.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ratings and review counts come from third parties (usually Google)
        when we have them. They are not our scores. A listing is not a
        recommendation. You choose who to call and what to check.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as-is. We do not warrant that listings are
        current, complete, or that a contractor is available, licensed,
        insured, or good at the job. We are not a party to any contract
        between you and a contractor. To the fullest extent allowed by law,
        {SITE_NAME} and its operator are not liable for hiring decisions,
        property damage, unpaid work, insurance disputes, or losses that
        come from using or not being able to use this site. Some states
        don’t allow certain limitations; those limits apply only as far as
        the law allows.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        We don’t require an account to browse. Favorites and a few UI hints
        (like whether you’ve seen the share tip) stay in your browser’s
        local storage on this device. We don’t sync those to a user profile.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you submit a listing request, we store what you send—typically
        business name, trade, city, phone, email, website, Google Business
        Profile link, and notes—so we can review and refresh the directory.
        We use that to operate the site, not to sell a list of homeowners or
        contractors. Hosting and database providers (including Convex) process
        that data for us.
      </p>
      <p>
        The public site shows business contact details that already appear
        (or reasonably appear) on public profiles. Clicking a contractor’s
        phone, email, website, or social link takes you to them—or to Google,
        L&amp;I, or another third party—with their own privacy practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        We don’t knowingly collect information from children under 13. This
        directory isn’t directed at them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this page. The “last updated” date at the top is the
        signal. Continued use after a change means you accept the new text.
        Questions:{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
